WEBVTT

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.030
Wow!

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.800
We're finally here.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.930
Yeah!

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.040
We should see it any minute!

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.110
There it is.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.330
Amazing...

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.870
This is the Holy Spring.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:59.150
<b>Episode 6 
The Holy Spring</b>

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.080
What a sight!

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.000
The angel's rings!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.420
Isn't it amazing?

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.990
Yeah... It really is.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.280
In the beginning, there was a single drop of rain.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.400
The drop fell for seven days and seven nights,

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.820
and on the eighth, it fell upon a flagstone.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.240
Isn't that the legend of Saint Aldista?

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:51.830
Yeah.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.810
The flagstone pitied the rain as it fell,

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.220
and Saint Aldista granted its wish.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:02.630
She created the Holy Spring, 
which shoots water high into the sky.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.220
I thought it was just a myth.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.380
I never imagined it was real.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:12.350
I wish my father could have seen it.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:14.910
And my mother.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.740
I have returned.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:27.440
Isla's true voyage begins.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.120
Who knows what we'll find?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.290
The enemy air force, shooting at us.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.490
You lack a sense of romance, Amelia...

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.970
I don't require one for my job.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.130
Very well, Foreign Secretary...

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.980
Has the captured pilot told us

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.380
anything of this enemy air force you speak of?

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.560
The Sky Clan's linguistic system

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.750
is very similar to that of Balsteros.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:54.410
It didn't take long for us to communicate.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.100
That of Balsteros?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:56.910
Yes.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.470
But at this point, all we know

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:04.990
is that they will attack anyone 
who enters the Holy Spring.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:09.020
Which means that we can't avoid combat...

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.500
They're simple barbarians.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:21.310
I've been enjoying the view 
with the foreign secretary.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.050
Thank you for the invitation,

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.770
Commander Leopold and 
Finance Secretary Marx.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.680
The Council of Four is all here.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:35.980
I was just speaking with the foreign 
secretary about the Sky Clan.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:41.980
What have we to fear from an enemy 
still using high-wing monoplanes?

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.650
We cannot fight an enemy if we 
know nothing about them.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.740
I'd like you to send out recon planes.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.030
We're already flying through uncharted territory.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.760
I don't want to frighten people.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:56.120
If you insist on doing it, why not use trainees?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.610
They may be barbarians, 
but I don't think the students...

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.930
Among the trainees is Nina—

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.360
Claire Cruz.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.540
Then simply don't send her.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.640
Come one, come all!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.560
It's delicious!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:15.160
I'd heard that the pilot trainees 
were running a restaurant.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.410
If you don't eat it, you'll be sorry!

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:16.920
What kind of restaurant is it?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:19.550
It's an Ari-men restaurant!

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.400
Ari-men?

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.950
Th-This is...

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.820
<i>A splendid soup, with a rich, subtle taste,</i>

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.330
<i>and delicious noodles that perfectly match it!</i>

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.250
<i>It's delicious!</i>

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:40.440
Is this Ari-men?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.000
The line ends here!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.260
H-Here you are.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.010
Welcome!

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.390
I'll read your order back to you.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:54.020
Three more Ari-men!

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.140
Got it!

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.640
When making noodles, 
the firmness is key.

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.460
Who's that?

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:10.450
We're in the same class, and you 
still don't know my name?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.700
I'm best friends with my bro, Wolf!

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.530
I'm Marco!

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.580
Who?

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.340
The Ari-men is really popular...

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:22.670
And we're making a lot of money.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:26.580
We won't lack anything for a while to come.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.670
We've sold more than 1,500,000 quills.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.970
It's incredible.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:34.170
Is the roast pork ramen ready yet?

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:34.800
Kal-el...

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.460
Huh? Where's Kal-el?

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.530
<i>We've finally made it this far...</i>

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.320
<i>I wonder what the End of the Sky is like.</i>

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:50.280
Ow!

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.040
Kal-el, don't slack off!

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.820
I'm not slacking off!

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.670
Everyone else is working hard.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.460
You have to work, too.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.600
We're running out of flour.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.350
And eggs and green onions.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:03.480
Okay, Sharon.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.460
Find someone who's free, and go with them.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.100
Want me to go?

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.960
You start cooking the pork!

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:19.120
It's like a huge festival.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.310
There used to be festivals like 
this in Benares, didn't there?

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.200
The Summer Solstice?

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.810
I remember that...

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.620
Excuse me!

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:31.390
Oh, you must be with Cadoques High.

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.760
Are you in the flight school?

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:33.450
Yes.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:36.520
Then you flew over the Holy Spring?

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.380
Yeah...

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.370
Oh, right.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:42.380
It's rumored that once you reach the 
Holy Spring, the Sky Clan will attack.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.570
Is that true?

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.720
Please take this, also.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.640
Um...

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:57.180
You look really good.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:03.040
A-Are you all right?

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.270
What should I do?

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.860
Did you hurt yourself?

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:09.150
No, I'm sorry.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:10.420
What's wrong?

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.920
Ari, get Claire patched up.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.150
Got it.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.460
Can I leave this to you for a while?

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:18.400
I don't mind.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.410
But aren't you the only one 
who can cook the noodles?

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:23.160
Um...

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.160
I'll do it!

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:29.140
I've watched her make Ari-men 
since she was a kid.

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:30.420
I think I can do it!

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.670
So you guys go and rest.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.170
Fine.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.080
Take care of it, then.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:38.720
Okay!

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.520
There we go.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.270
Thanks...

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.030
Since all that was new to you, you must be tired.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:55.240
No, you must be more tired...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.420
You're so amazing.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:59.240
You can do anything.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.320
That isn't true...

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.870
My older sisters taught me.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.610
I wonder how everyone 
is doing right now...

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.710
I'm sure they're fine.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.680
They're looking forward to 
you two coming home!

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:16.970
That's right.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.340
I'm worried about Kal, 
so I'm going to head back.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.620
You want to rest a little more?

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:24.540
No...

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.980
I'll go back, as well.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.500
Relax a bit...

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.270
I'm on my last legs, too.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.720
How did this happen?

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:37.070
But I'm happy that the 
Ari-men is so popular...

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:39.820
It's so delicious!

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.270
I know I messed up back there,

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.450
and I know I don't live at the dorm,

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.510
but since everyone else is working 
so hard for the sake of the dorm,

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:49.840
I'll also do my best!

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.930
Then let's go back together.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.430
Again?

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.340
Huh? That isn't right?

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:05.680
It's exactly what we all expected...

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:06.970
What's wrong?

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.960
The line of customers keeps increasing.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.190
And people are complaining that 
the noodles are too soft.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:14.860
Fine...

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:16.780
Let me see it!

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:19.070
Then, I'll try.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.790
J-Just let me do it.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.070
Move.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:25.970
I didn't know you were here.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:29.150
Your sister dragged me here.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:30.520
Stop it...

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:31.710
It's impossible.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.630
I was watching her as I washed plates.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.000
I have the basics down.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.370
It's perfect.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.650
You're really talented, Ignacio!

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:48.640
Amazing, Igna!

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.780
If we do this together,
 we can knock it out fast.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.650
Yeah, you're really good!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.300
Kal,

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:58.150
we don't need you here anymore, 
so go back and help customers.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.120
Claire, show him how.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:06.280
First, get everyone a pair of chopsticks 
and a glass of water.

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:08.300
Say, "Welcome,"

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.760
take their order, and return.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.080
When it's ready, bring it out.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:16.190
And when they finish, ask, "May I take this?"

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:19.340
Was that hard to understand?

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.970
No, I've got it perfectly!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.680
Want to try it, then?

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.560
Yeah!

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:31.680
Thank you!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.770
The food was great.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.520
Thank you!

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:39.270
Sharon said the people in town 
were talking about a rumor.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.690
About what?

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:44.250
They said when we enter the Spring, 
the Sky Clan will attack us.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.900
Well, we thought they were just a fairy tale,

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.330
so it was a big surprise when they really existed.

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.080
But it's said they use old planes...

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.580
It'll be just fine.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.300
Two Ari-men...

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.720
One large-sized, right?

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.890
Here you are.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.350
It's hot, so be careful.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.970
Enjoy.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:17.580
Admiral?

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:21.610
I'm glad to see your student life is going well.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.380
The Ari-men is really good...

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.450
Enjoy yourself.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.410
You don't have a curfew tonight.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.200
I've spoken to Countess Ulshyrra.

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:33.660
Have fun.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.790
Thank you very much!

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.310
Hey!

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:44.630
It's been a long time.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.710
Bandereas, what are you doing?

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:51.180
Navigation Officer Luis...

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.320
Navigation Officer? Ha!

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:56.810
He's a coward who was terrified by the 
sound of guns and played dead—

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.650
I am Sonia Palez, an instructor here!

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:04.880
Honored to meet you, Admiral Luis.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.380
The pleasure is mine, Instructor Sonia...

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.660
Would you please stop saluting?

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.960
Make the pain stop!

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.530
I'm here in secrecy.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.630
If someone learns who I am, 
there'll be trouble.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.660
I'm sorry, sir.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:24.100
I've known this gorilla since we were 
naval trainees, back in our teens.

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:27.670
I don't need any fancy greetings. 
Just have a seat.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.140
Thank you, sir.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.010
Here you are, instructor!

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.010
We haven't ordered yet.

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:37.850
It's our treat.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.730
Enjoy yourselves.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.840
Let's eat, then.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:43.860
Yes, let's.

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.530
Thanks for coming!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.140
Difficult to believe a student made this.

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:56.540
It is a surprise...

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.350
Sonia, are you okay?

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:04.210
Y-Yes, Admiral.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:08.400
You looked as if something had 
stolen your heart away.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.280
It was wonderful.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:15.660
I'd like a chance to learn more about you...

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:19.600
You haven't changed, you bastard!

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.630
And you? Are you actually doing your job?

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:25.100
I'm sure it won't be long before you 
punch the principal or a student

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:26.870
in the face and get fired.

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:28.440
I don't punch people!

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:31.240
You knocked out a rear admiral 
when you were a low-ranking officer.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.240
I could see you punching anyone.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.700
You knocked out a rear admiral?!

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:39.090
In his defense, the gorilla did have a point.

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:43.640
The admiral had ordered a series of 
long-range bombings without escort

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.960
that cost the lives of many pilots.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:49.170
He'd gone to ask the admiral 
to reconsider, but...

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:52.180
He wouldn't talk to me, 
so I had no choice.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:55.490
The only reason he wasn't executed 
was that he happened to be

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:58.470
the Royal Air Defense's ace.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.930
He was an imperial ace?

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.700
Forget that!

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:08.150
I'm more interested in how you'll be using 
my students for recon missions.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:11.780
Commander Leopold's request...

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:18.200
Even if they enemy uses outdated equipment, 
you'd still send students into a war zone?

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:26.910
I'm praying it won't be a war zone...

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:32.620
You don't think the Sky Clan will 
be mere barbarians, do you?

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.640
That's why I strengthened Isla's defenses.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:43.000
I'd rather not use young people 
likely to be as crazy as you.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:48.610
Tell the student who made it 
that the Ari-men was delicious.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:17:01.510
Total sales for the evening are 1,786,500 quill.

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:03.210
An amazing evening!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.710
Wow!

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.730
Everyone worked really hard...

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:07.460
Right?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.180
Making the noodles was very tough.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:13.080
My face is stuck in a smile...

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:15.340
But it's all thanks to Ari, isn't it?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:19.130
Good work today... Truly, Ari.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:22.320
I'm never making Ari-men again.

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:23.980
Huh? Why?

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.830
Because I want to be a pilot...

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:29.660
At this rate, I'm likely to end up a ramen chef.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:31.900
Right, Chiharu?

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.330
Y-Yeah.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.740
You're amazing... You can do anything.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.150
I can't do anything!

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:41.580
Your practical scores are better 
than mine, Chiharu...

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:42.930
Um, Chiharu...

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.250
No, it's thanks to my partner.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.790
Not at all.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.450
I'm the one who needs help.

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:52.950
Mitty knows all about airplanes 
and machine guns...

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.320
And he's good at using them.

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:55.930
He's great to have around!

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:57.050
Good to hear.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.570
I don't see it...

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:02.430
I think Chiharu would get along 
with anyone she was paired with...

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.120
That isn't true!

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.660
Just Mitty...

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:07.930
Because Mitty is amazing.

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:08.850
Chiharu?

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.810
Come on, he's just way too into airplanes...

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.670
He isn't funny, and he's fat.

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.290
That's the only thing he's good at.

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:19.170
It's amazing that he has even 
one thing he's good at.

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:23.280
I don't have anything I'm good at...

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:24.950
I...

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.390
Chiharu?

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:30.210
This isn't like you.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.920
U-Um...

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:33.840
Is something wrong?

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:35.120
Kal!

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:36.060
Listen...

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:40.260
All I did was say Mitsuo was way 
too into airplanes, and then...

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.750
Yeah, he is.

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:43.430
Isn't he?

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:46.250
He knows more about airplanes than anyone,

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:49.190
and his piloting and recon skills are amazing!

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:50.770
N-No...

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:53.510
Eh? What?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:55.330
Did I say something weird?

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:56.110
No...

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.940
I don't even feel like being mad anymore.

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:07.620
Okay, then let's have a party of our own!

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:09.580
Yeah!

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:17.800
How did I end up looking like the bad guy?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.840
What? Why?

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:23.340
Damn it, you don't understand anything!

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:26.680
Kal isn't so bad himself.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.210
Even when he couldn't do it, he took my place.

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:44.700
Mitty?

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.200
Want to sit down?

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:47.110
Sure.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:55.560
Oh, thanks for what you said earlier.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.970
For defending me.

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:00.100
I just said what I think.

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:02.180
You really are amazing, Mitty.

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:05.610
I don't have anything that makes me special.

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:06.840
That's not true...

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:08.810
Your piloting's a lot more stable now.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:10.790
And you work really hard.

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.500
Thanks.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:16.940
You're the first person to ever say that.

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:21.800
My mom always used to tell me I was no good...

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:24.630
Even though my older and younger 
brothers could do anything.

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:28.230
So I thought that if I could fly, it would be nice!

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:29.870
That's why I came to Isla.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:32.400
Kind of a lame motive, isn't it?

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:35.330
Like I'm running from something.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.620
That isn't true!

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:39.420
Coming here was the only 
thing I could be good at.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.690
I'm...

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:43.880
really glad you came.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.090
I tried to cheer you up,

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:49.600
and instead, you cheered me up.

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:53.590
I'm glad we could see the Holy Spring together.

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:55.490
Yeah, it was amazing.

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:58.480
Just seeing it made coming here worth it.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:02.920
But they say that, once we 
reach the Holy Spring,

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:03.990
the Sky Clan will attack.

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:07.170
That's the rumor going around, isn't it?

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:08.840
Will we have to fight them?

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:11.200
I'll be there!

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.400
Like everyone says,

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:16.300
all I'm good at is piloting and shooting, so...

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:21.490
Hold my hand.

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:30.310
Your hand is warm...

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:32.390
So is yours.

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:42.100
I hope we can all fly these skies forever.

00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:32.950
It's me, Ignacio.

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:34.810
We've been given the order to launch.

00:23:34.810 --> 00:23:37.700
His mission is AA support.

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:40.140
Well, if that idiot went out there, 
he'd just get in—

00:23:39.950 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Episode 7 
A Glorious Death</b>
